{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.ns_singularity_descartes","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.ns_singularity_descartes","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.ns_singularity_descartes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.ns_singularity_descartes","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/ns_singularity_descartes.lean#L41-L50","doc":"**NS-singularity of the Descartes universe** ([`thm:ns-singularity-descartes`]).\n\nWith `χ(A) = -6` the NS obstruction is non-zero.  The singularity\nconclusion is *derived* from the Euler characteristic via\n`obstruction_from_chi`, not asserted. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:ns-singularity-descartes","label":"thm:ns-singularity-descartes","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-singularity-descartes.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NsSingularityDescartesContext.obstruction_from_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NsSingularityDescartesContext.obstruction_from_chi","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/ns_singularity_descartes.lean#L39-L39","doc":"**Obstruction survival (deep):** `χ(A) = -6` forces a non-vanishing NS\nobstruction — `-6` is not divisible by `2κ` for `κ ≥ 4`, so the\ntopological obstruction in `H²(S, G_m)/2κ` persists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NsSingularityDescartesContext.chi_A_is_neg_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NsSingularityDescartesContext.chi_A_is_neg_six","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/ns_singularity_descartes.lean#L35-L35","doc":"**Setup:** the Descartes universe has Euler characteristic `-6`\n(Bring's surface, genus 4). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NsSingularityDescartesContext.chi_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NsSingularityDescartesContext.chi_A","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/ns_singularity_descartes.lean#L32-L32","doc":"The Euler characteristic `χ(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NsSingularityDescartesContext.NS_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NsSingularityDescartesContext.NS_A","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/ns_singularity_descartes.lean#L30-L30","doc":"The NS obstruction `NS(A) = e(ξ)|_Σ` (Euler class restricted to the\ncollision locus). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NsSingularityDescartesContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NsSingularityDescartesContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/ns_singularity_descartes.lean#L27-L27","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NsSingularityDescartesContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NsSingularityDescartesContext","kind":"class","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/ns_singularity_descartes.lean#L25-L39","doc":"Hypotheses for NS-singularity of the Descartes universe (§7c: generic\n`CommRing`, `ℤ` Euler characteristic, no `ℝ`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}